In BBj 14.00 and higher, this method gets the full name and path location
for the temporary file has been stored in a [BBjFileUpload](https://documentation.basis.cloud/BASISHelp/WebHelp/bbjobjects/Servlet/bbjfileupload/BBjFileUpload.htm)
object.[Docs](https://documentation.basis.cloud/BASISHelp/WebHelp/bbjobjects/Servlet/bbjfileupload/BBjFileUpload_getTempName.htm)

In BBj 11.00 and higher, this method returns
the [BBjSessionInfo](https://documentation.basis.cloud/BASISHelp/WebHelp/bbjobjects/API/bbjsessioninfo/bbjsessioninfo.htm) object
for the current session.[Docs](https://documentation.basis.cloud/BASISHelp/WebHelp/bbjobjects/bbjapi/bbjapi_getcurrentsessioninfo.htm)

In BBj 12.00 and higher, this method returns the specified header value
from the [BBjHttpRequest](https://documentation.basis.cloud/BASISHelp/WebHelp/bbjobjects/Servlet/bbjhttprequest/bbjhttprequest.htm)
object.[Docs](https://documentation.basis.cloud/BASISHelp/WebHelp/bbjobjects/Servlet/bbjhttprequest/BBjHttpRequest_getHeader.htm)

In BBj 12.00 and higher, this method returns the name and version of
the protocol the request uses in the form protocol/majorVersion.minorVersion,
for example, HTTP/1.1.[Docs](https://documentation.basis.cloud/BASISHelp/WebHelp/bbjobjects/Servlet/bbjhttprequest/BBjHttpRequest_getProtocol.htm)

In BBj 12.00 and higher, this method returns the name of the scheme used
to make this request in the [BBjHttpRequest](https://documentation.basis.cloud/BASISHelp/WebHelp/bbjobjects/Servlet/bbjhttprequest/bbjhttprequest.htm),
for example, HTTP, HTTPS, or FTP.[Docs](https://documentation.basis.cloud/BASISHelp/WebHelp/bbjobjects/Servlet/bbjhttprequest/BBjHttpRequest_getScheme.htm)
